<statement>
<p>
	This function will run the &quot;color decoder&quot; game. You may wish to use some of the functions you&#x27;ve created up to this point.
</p>

<tabular valign="top" top="minor">
	<col width="12%"/>
	<col width="88%"/>
	<row bottom="minor">
		<cell>Inputs:</cell>
		<cell>
			<p><pf>num_attempts</pf> (double) double — is the maximum number of guesses the user is allowed</p>
			<p><pf>color_list</pf> number — is a string of 6 letters representing 6 among the standard colors MATLAB recognizes:</p>
			<p><pf>'b'</pf> number — = blue, <pf>'k'</pf> = black, <pf>'r'</pf> = red, <pf>'g'</pf> = green, <pf>'y'</pf> = yellow, <pf>'c'</pf> = cyan, <pf>'m'</pf> = magenta, <pf>'w'</pf> = white</p>
		</cell>
	</row>
	<row bottom="minor">
		<cell>Outputs:</cell>
		<cell>
			<p><pf>no</pf> number — function outputs</p>
		</cell>
	</row>
	<row>
		<cell>Details:</cell>
		<cell><p>Do not attempt to code the entire game at once. Write a line or two of code, then test it, and repeat.</p></cell>
	</row>
	<row>
		<cell/>
		<cell><p>While you are testing, you might want to keep num_attempts small.</p></cell>
	</row>
	<row bottom="minor">
		<cell/>
		<cell><p>While you are testing, you might want to reveal the secret code at the top of the game board. This will allow you to be able to visually check whether the feedback is appropriate for the given secret code.</p></cell>
	</row>
</tabular>

</statement>
